  "layout": "director",
  "panel_title": "Flash H3 Director",
  "notes": "The panel builds a native H3 timeline: each window has its own prompt and ordered reference pictures/audio. ref2va uses the reference model (give it at least one picture or clip); fl2va uses the text/first-last model (leave both endpoint assignments empty for plain text-to-video). Each FL2VA window accepts first_frame and last_frame as optional zero-based Picture bin slots; they condition the endpoints and are not Ref2VA references. 8 steps, euler, SLA 0.80 and multiple 32 are studio-managed. The Production recipe has been rendered; start with one 7.3 s segment. Build & Test runs at 0.1 MP with RelayVSR off; Production defaults to 0.3 MP with its own remembered resolution and RelayVSR x2. Switching profiles never changes the timeline, prompts, references or seed, and never starts a render. A succeeded preview can be promoted to Production from the history; the production request keeps the preview's exact creative payload, and both jobs stay linked in the history. The published gallery example is a single 15 s segment from the measured h3-video-flash run (same Flash H3 model stack), not a multi-segment director render. Qwen3.8 Heretic prompt enhancement is enabled by default; it rewrites every Material Planner segment in order, feeding previous scenes as context and using each segment's ordered pictures/clips.",
